cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Cellular composition shifts dominate the COVID-19 brain
  transcriptomic response: code and analysis pipeline
message: >-
  If you use this code or data, please cite both the
  associated manuscript and this repository.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Kelechi
    family-names: Elechi
    name-particle: Wisdom
    email: kelechiwisdom20@gmail.com
    affiliation: >-
      Sam and Ann Barshop Institute for Longevity and Aging
      Studies, University of Texas Health Science Center at
      San Antonio
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-0691-4180"
repository-code: "https://github.com/kelyto30/covid-brain-aging-thesis"
url: "https://github.com/kelyto30/covid-brain-aging-thesis"
abstract: >-
  Analytical pipeline for the dissertation manuscript
  "Cellular composition shifts dominate the COVID-19 brain
  transcriptomic response: NF-kB, IFN/JAK-STAT and REST
  master regulators converge on a five-cell-type neurovascular
  signature in postmortem frontal cortex." Re-analyses the
  GSE188847 frontal-cortex bulk RNA-seq cohort (n = 54) using
  DESeq2 differential expression, clusterProfiler GSEA, VIPER
  master regulator analysis with DoRothEA regulons, BRETIGEA
  cell-type deconvolution, and composition-corrected
  differential expression.
keywords:
  - COVID-19
  - brain aging
  - transcriptomics
  - master regulator analysis
  - cell-type deconvolution
  - VIPER
  - BRETIGEA
  - DoRothEA
  - bulk RNA-seq
  - postmortem brain
license: MIT
